# Docker build-context excludes for backend/Dockerfile (PSY-1790).
#
# WHY IT LIVES HERE, NOT AT THE REPO ROOT. Docker reads `.dockerignore` from
# the root of the build CONTEXT, and both builds of this image use `backend/`
# as the context:
#   * CI      — .github/workflows/backend-image.yml sets `context: ./backend`
#   * Railway — the service's root directory is /backend, and railway.toml's
#               `dockerfilePath = "Dockerfile"` resolves inside it.
# A repo-root .dockerignore would be read by NEITHER, and would fail silently.
#
# DENY-LIST, DELIBERATELY. The builder stage runs `COPY . .` and then
# `go build ./cmd/server`, so the entire Go tree has to arrive. An allow-list
# would silently drop the next package someone adds, and the break would
# surface as a compile error in CI rather than as a missing rule here. Only
# paths the build provably does not need are listed below.
#
# NEVER add an entry that matches any of these — the build needs them:
#   **/*.go, go.mod, go.sum          the module the builder compiles
#   db/migrations/                   COPYd into the runtime stage
#   layout/                          npm ci + fa2-layout.mjs (layout-deps stage)
#   docker-entrypoint.sh             the image's ENTRYPOINT
#   internal/services/geo/data/      go:embed cities.tsv / countries.tsv, ~11MB
#                                    compiled INTO the binary (geo.go)
# In particular, do NOT reach for a blanket `*.sql`: db/migrations/ is SQL.

# Go coverage profiles. Written by scripts/coverage.sh and by CI's
# `go test -coverprofile=...`; never an input to anything. Same rule as the
# repo .gitignore's `backend/**/*.out`.
**/*.out
**/*.cov
coverage.html

# Local database dumps and backups. `backup_*.tar.gz` and
# `psychicdb_dump_*.sql` are still tracked in git (out of scope for PSY-1790,
# noted as a follow-up); the rest are untracked local droppings. These
# patterns are anchored so they cannot reach db/migrations/.
backups/
backup_*.tar.gz
*_dump_*.sql
*.dump

# Environment files. The image takes its configuration from the platform's
# environment at runtime, so nothing here is read at build time and shipping a
# real .env into a layer would be a credential leak.
.env*

# Local orchestration and host provisioning. Compose brings up dev/e2e/stage
# stacks from OUTSIDE the image, and systemd units target VMs, not containers.
docker-compose*.yml
systemd/

# Docs. Prose only; no build stage reads it.
docs/
*.md

# Editor / OS droppings that would otherwise bust the context cache.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# A locally-installed dependency tree. The layout-deps stage runs its own
# `npm ci` from package.json + package-lock.json, so a host node_modules is
# both unused and (being built for the host arch) wrong.
**/node_modules/
